{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119951","id":3783873713,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7hiVSx","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119951","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119951.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119951.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119951","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119951/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119951/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119951/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3036a22353db02fe22f18450e5737de62f056e1f","number":119951,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"C#: Add roslyn analyzer for parameterless constructors","user":{"login":"ryanslikesocool","id":29644580,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjQ0NTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29644580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool","html_url":"https://github.com/ryanslikesocool","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryanslikesocool/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\r\nThis PR adds a C# analyzer that warns programmers when declaring a class inheriting from `GodotObject` that does not declare a parameterless constructor.\r\nParameterless constructors are a requirement for C# classes inheriting from `GodotObject`.  Documentation relating to it is not front-and-center (I would expect to find it under [C# API differences to GDScript][csharp-api-differences-to-gdscript], [Current Gotchas and Known Issues][current-gotchas-and-known-issues], or [Common Pitfalls][common-pitfalls]).  Crashes caused by not declaring parameterless constructors do not provide easily-diagnosable errors.\r\n\r\nFrom the [official documentation][creating-your-own-resources] (first code example under the C# tab):\r\n> Make sure you provide a parameterless constructor.\r\n> In C#, a parameterless constructor is different from a constructor with all default values.\r\n> Without a parameterless constructor, Godot will have problems creating and editing your resource via the inspector.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n- Add analyzer and diagnostic in `Godot.SourceGenerators`\r\n- Add code fix provider that adds a parameterless constructor\r\n- Add tests in `Godot.SourceGenerators.Tests`\r\n\r\n## Example\r\n```cs\r\n// This will not emit a warning because the class does not inherit from `GodotObject`\r\nclass MyObject1 {\r\n  public MyObject1(int value) { /* ... */ }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// This will not emit a warning because the class does not declare any constructors\r\npartial class MyObject2 : Node { }\r\n\r\n// This will not emit a warning because the class declares a parameterless constructor\r\npartial class MyObject3 : Node {\r\n  public MyObject3() { /* ... */ }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// This will not emit a warning because the class declares a parameterless constructor\r\npartial class MyObject4 : Node {\r\n  public MyObject4() { /* ... */ }\r\n\r\n  public MyObject4(int value) { /* ... */ }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// This WILL emit a warning because the class does not declare a parameterless constructor\r\npartial class MyObject5 : Node {\r\n  public MyObject5(int value) { /* ... */ }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Concerns\r\n- I gave the diagnostic the ID `GD0004`, since it is related to class declarations like `GD0001` - `GD0003`.\r\nThere may be a more appropriate ID to give it.\r\n- I made the diagnostic a warning, not an error like all other analyzers.\r\nI can't imagine a situation where this *isn't* an error, but there may be a legitimate use that I don't know about.\r\n\r\n[csharp-api-differences-to-gdscript]: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_differences.html\r\n[current-gotchas-and-known-issues]: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.html#current-gotchas-and-known-issues\r\n[common-pitfalls]: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/c_sharp/c_sharp_basics.html#common-pitfalls\r\n[creating-your-own-resources]: https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/scripting/resources.html#creating-your-own-resources","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":709269775,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MDkyNjk3NzU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:dotnet","name":"topic:dotnet","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.gith